ended N.I.N.A. imaging nights and post each image with its acquisition numbers (AstroBin, NINA Discord).\",\n708-  \"problem\": [\n709-    \"Every finished image is posted with typed numbers. An observatory page lists \\\"RGBHaSIIOIII = 360:340:335:725:720:715 (53.25hours)\\\"; another gives \\\"SII 15 x 10 min., Ha 10 x 10 min., OIII 20 x 10 min.\\\" in a prose block.\",\n710-    \"The numbers already exist: the NINA Session Metadata plugin writes one ImageMetaData.csv row per frame, since NINA's own FITS headers are \\\"not really convenient to access for a set of images\\\". Other tools read these files, and one imager built a log analyzer because the overnight log is \\\"hard-to-read\\\".\",\n711-    \"No thread asking for this exact picture was found, and AstroBin could not be read: the demand is inferred from the hand-typed blocks.\"\n712-  ],\n713-  \"sources\": [\n714-    \"https://github.com/tcpalmer/nina.plugin.sessionmetadata\",\n715-    \"https://www.ideviceapps.de/NINAImageAnalysisHandbook/\",\n716-    \"https://scopetrader.com/nina-log-analyzer/\",\n717-    \"https://skycenter.arizona.edu/astrophotography/m57-ring-nebula\",\n718-    \"https://sdspacegrant.sdsmt.edu/PacmanNebula-RichardWalker.htm\"\n719-  ],\n720-  \"solution\": [\n721-    \"The CSV is the prop. Paste ImageMetaData.csv into csv (only FilterName, ExposureStartUTC and Duration are read) or pass rows of { night, filter, frames, exposureSec }. One bar per filter on ONE scale fixed from the first frame, each bar stacked from a segment per night.\",\n722-    \"The clip opens on the finished card, lets the nights land in order with a running total, and ends where it began. Seconds are summed whole and rounded once for display; a dual-band filter is counted as named, never split.\",\n723-    \"Weak spots: no image, the filter colours are a taste call, and a night is any run of frames with no 6 h gap.\"\n724-  ],\n725-  \"usage\": {\n726-    \"command\": \"m0saic make @one-a-day/science/astro-integration-summary/v1 --template-repo . -w 1920 -h 1080 -o summary.mp4\",\n727-    \"try\": [\n728-      \"--props @props.json with {\\\"csv\\\": \\\"<your ImageMetaData.csv>\\\"} - your own nights\",\n729-      \"sessions - rows of { night, filter, frames, exposureSec } typed by hand\",\n730-      \"filterColors {\\\"Ha\\\":\\\"#ff5533\\\"} for your palette; footer \\\"\\\" drops the invented-data line\",\n731-      \"-w 1080 -h 1920 for a story; --durationMs 8000 for a shorter clip\"\n732-    ]\n733-  },\n734-  \"caveats\": [\n735-    \"Demand is inferred from hand-typed blocks, not quoted from a thread asking for this picture.\",\n736-    \"Dual-band filters are counted as named (one row each); nothing is split into channels.\",\n737-    \"The hours are drawtext in the machine's font; pixels are deterministic per machine only.\"\n738-  ],\n739-  \"timeline\": {\n740-    \"source\": \"runner\",\n741-    \"phases\": [\n742-      {\n743-        \"name\": \"scout\",\n744-        \"startMs\": 0,\n745-        \"durMs\": 262206,\n746-        \"calls\": 37,\n747-        \"tokens\": 3491066,\n748-        \"costUsd\": 1,\n749-        \"tools\": \"Bash 16, WebSearch 16, WebFetch 2\"\n750-      },\n751-      {\n--\n1096:  return withLayoutIntent(doc, ctx, { templateId: ID, constraints: layoutContract(L), relations: model.filters.length >= 2 ? trackRelations : [], debug: props.debugLayout === true });\n1097-}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8e7ecac-0750-4994-8166-6c4f4b9f2cae","uuid":"23b4f2b7-74ab-464f-ab1f-22701fb73d2a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:56:18.263Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"mode\": \"gate\",\n  \"templates\": 23,\n  \"rendered\": 23,\n  \"skipped\": [],\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    {\n      \"templateId\": \"@one-a-day/social/episode-audiogram/v1\",\n      \"convention\": \"costBudget\",\n      \"severity\": \"warning\",\n      \"violations\": [\n        {\n          \"key\": \"overlayDepth\",\n